APPENDIX  “A”
PEAK WELLNESS CENTER, INC.
ALCOHOL RECEIVING CENTER
Mission:
To provide social, non-medical alcohol and drug detoxification services for the well-
being and safety of those in need and for the community in general.
TOTAL BUDGET %
# OF CLIENTS BENEFITTED
FUNDING REQUEST
OF THE REQUEST
OR STATISTICS
City of Cheyenne
42.3
444 clients
$84,955.00
1,478 client days
Service:
The primary purpose of the Alcohol Receiving Center is to provide a supportive and recovery
oriented setting to assist clients to safely detoxify from alcohol and other drugs of abuse.  Inherent
in this purpose is the order and welfare of the community at large, including judicial use of law
enforcement facilities and other resources.
The Center attempts to keep clients beyond the initial detoxification period, three to five days, to
encourage them to engage in ongoing substance abuse treatment.  As a result, we have seen more of
them enter outpatient or residential treatment with a consequent reduction in repeat detoxification
admissions.
The Center is open and staffed for admissions 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, throughout the year.
Clients are monitored every 15 minutes and are taken by staff or ambulance for emergency medical
care as needed.  Meals and other sustenance are provided as well as referrals for shelter, medical and
mental health care, employment, AA and NA, and other supportive resources.
